redict: compilation/import error because `game-of-life.ts` doesn't exist. Then after creating stub, runtime assertion error. \n\nHmm, vitest run with a missing module: the test file `import { nextGeneration } from \"./game-of-life.js\"` — vitest will throw \"Failed to resolve import\" and the test errors out (not a clean assertion fail, but an error). That counts as the test failing for the right reason (missing impl). Good. Prediction: \"Test fails because module './game-of-life.js' cannot be resolved.\" Correct.\n\nLet me now write everything. First, the test list file with it.todo() entries. Then immediately proceed to Red for test 1.\n\nLet me write the test file `src/game-of-life.spec.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { nextGeneration } from \"./game-of-life.js\";\n\ntype Cell = [number, number];\n\ndescribe(\"Game of Life - Next Generation\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"empty input returns empty -- [] -> []\");\n  it.todo(\"block still life is unchanged (live cells with 3 neighbors survive) -- [(0,0),(1,0),(0,1),(1,1)] -> same\");\n  it.todo(\"single live cell with 0 neighbors dies (underpopulation) -- [(0,0)] -> []\");\n  it.todo(\"two adjacent live cells each with 1 neighbor die (underpopulation) -- [(0,1),(1,1)] -> []\");\n  it.todo(\"live cell with more than 3 neighbors dies (overpopulation) -- 2x3 rectangle -> corners survive, middles die, wings born\");\n  it.todo(\"dead cell with exactly 3 live neighbors becomes alive (reproduction) -- [(0,0),(1,0),(0,1)] -> [(0,0),(0,1),(1,0),(1,1)]\");\n  it.todo(\"blinker oscillator: vertical line becomes horizontal -- [(0,0),(0,1),(0,2)] -> [(-1,1),(0,1),(1,1)]\");\n  it.todo(\"blinker returns to original after two generations -- [(0,0),(0,1),(0,2)] -> [(0,0),(0,1),(0,2)]\");\n  it.todo(\"handles negative coordinates: block at negative coords unchanged -- [(-1,-1),(0,-1),(-1,0),(0,0)] -> same\");\n});\n```\n\nWait — the `type Cell` import: the spec defines `type Cell = [number, number]